      <qti-content-body>
        <p>In which of these sentences is <strong>wrath</strong> used correctly?</p>
        <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">She felt a flash of wrath when her pencil rolled off the desk during the quiz.</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="B">His wrath at the slow traffic melted away the moment the light turned green.</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="C">The coach's wrath after the betrayal was so fierce that players feared practice for weeks.</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The librarian's gentle wrath reminded the students to whisper politely.</qti-simple-choice>
        </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
